00:04:59.939 --> 00:05:03.079
Reading a 3% contract starts with what the price is buying.

00:05:03.079 --> 00:05:09.159
saying. Yes pays $1 if the event resolves yes and nothing if it resolves no. Three cents

00:05:09.159 --> 00:05:14.619
for that dollar is a 3% price. It is not this show saying the event will happen, and it

00:05:14.619 --> 00:05:19.979
is not a side to take. Flip the contract. Yes, at 3 cents is the same quote as no near

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:26.459
97 cents, when the two payoffs add to a dollar. The yes buyer parks 3 cents until resolution.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:30.079
The no-buyer parks about 97 cents for the same weight.

00:05:30.499 --> 00:05:32.159
That weight is the time value.

00:05:32.619 --> 00:05:36.519
Cash in the favorite cannot move to another question until the rules say the contract

00:05:36.519 --> 00:05:37.019
is done.

00:05:37.719 --> 00:05:40.059
A fee bites harder on 3 cents than on 50.

00:05:40.679 --> 00:05:45.519
The same charge is a large share of a long-shot stake and a small share of a coin flip stake.

00:05:46.019 --> 00:05:50.419
So the screen price and the return someone keeps are different numbers, and the gap is

00:05:50.419 --> 00:05:51.259
wider in the tail.

00:05:51.259 --> 00:05:56.699
At $0.50, both sides lock similar cash and a fee is a similar fraction of either.

00:05:57.199 --> 00:06:02.579
At $0.3, the displayed chance, the cash stock, and the fees share of that cash pull apart.

00:06:03.159 --> 00:06:06.079
A basket of rare events can each print at a few cents.

00:06:06.619 --> 00:06:11.599
If people buy them like lottery tickets, a small stake for a dollar, the price can sit above

00:06:11.599 --> 00:06:16.259
how often those events actually hit, and no single contract looks absurd alone.

00:06:16.859 --> 00:06:21.379
Sellers of that cheap side may also want extra pay for the rare chance the favorite loses

00:06:21.379 --> 00:06:21.979
everything.

00:06:22.579 --> 00:06:26.079
Either pressure means 3 cents is a price, not a clean frequency.

00:06:26.679 --> 00:06:32.099
When you see 3%, name the venue, notice whether the stake is dollars or play money, and

00:06:32.099 --> 00:06:35.299
remember 97 cents is the other chair at the same table.

00:06:35.899 --> 00:06:37.799
None of that is a reason to buy or sell.

